  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_029 (multimodal, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) achieved 0.6287 acc, outperforming the RNA-only baseline config_003 (0.5907 acc) by ~3.8%, confirming that adding the image modality with these encoders is beneficial. However, we have no information on whether the fusion strategy (concat vs. weighted) meaningfully affects performance. Question: config_043 is identical to config_029 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, cleanly isolating the effect of the fusion mechanism while holding RNA encoder, image encoder, profile setting, and aggregation constant. Why this is the best next step: it is a single-variable exploitation of the best-performing configuration, directly tests whether the two modalities contribute unequally (which weighted fusion would capture), and the result will inform whether all future multimodal experiments should use concat or weighted fusion. Under a limited budget, this clean A/B comparison maximizes information per experiment without confounding multiple design changes."
}

